-- An annotation written on the line where a clause ends, after its body, stays
-- with that clause, as it does after a rule written as one definition. It was
-- taken by the next clause, which published the second of two overloads under
-- an @export written on the first's line, and drew the first overload's @nlg
-- when the second was called (refutation of legalese/l4-ide#545's review,
-- round 4).

-- Two overloads, told apart by their types. Neither is published, and neither
-- takes the @nlg: calls to both render as calls to `g`.
DECIDE f n IS n + 1 @export inline on the first overload's line
DECIDE f b IS b AND TRUE

DECIDE g n IS n + 1 @nlg inline on the first overload's line
DECIDE g b IS b AND TRUE

-- A group, with an @desc, an @nlg and an @export after the bodies of its first
-- three clauses: none is "above the second clause", or the third.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE grouped 0 IS 1 @desc inline after the first body
DECIDE grouped 1 IS 2 @nlg inline after the second body
DECIDE grouped 2 IS 3 @export inline after the third body
DECIDE grouped other IS 4

#EVAL f 3
#EVAL f TRUE
#EVAL g 3
#EVAL g TRUE
#EVAL grouped 1
